			<div class="content" id="post-content-1492445">
									

<p>Firstly, I'm glad you started with a clean slate to a new article.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A perimeter of 50<br />
only males age 35<br />
After three (3)<br />
After one (1) month</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm confused at the number inconsistency. Either one or the other, both is unnecessary.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Any murmuring observed after this point will consist only of the Irish word for “happy” again and again.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't get it. I don't believe Irish is a language. Gaelic maybe?</p>
<p>I'm far too tired to go into a more extensive review, but the article has some tone issues. Overall, I kind of like the idea of deluding a man so the building can repair itself to its own needs (which is why I wrote 1551, lol) but there are little details that are annoying. Also, the article itself doesn't do very much to me. I don't hate it, but I don't feel anything.</p>

